    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.ui.input` can cause self-cascading when called from a keymap resulting in the input being fed into each cursor position. The check with ~~`vim.api.nvim__mcursor_cascading`~~ `vim.v.cascading` is bypassed. Interestingly, calling `vim.notify(\"+Self-Cascading\", vim.log.levels.ERROR)` can prevent this.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ee23458-1ee0-4744-8c06-dc490786010d\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nlocal ns_mc = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace(\"nvim.multicursor\")\nvim.bo.follow = true\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<F1>\", function()\n  if vim.v.cascading then\n    -- `vim.log.levels.ERROR` prevents feeding keys\n    vim.notify(\"+Self-Cascading\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    return\n  end\n  vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { 1, 0 })\n  local input_opts = { prompt = \"Match: \" }\n  vim.ui.input(input_opts, function(input)\n    vim.fn.setreg(\"/\", input)\n    local pos = vim.pos.cursor()\n    while vim.fn.search(input, \"W\") > 0 do\n      pos = vim.pos.cursor()\n      vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(pos.buf, ns_mc, pos.row, pos.col, {})\n    end\n  end)\nend)\n```\n\n```\nnvim --clean -u repro.lua repro.lua\n<F1>input<Enter>\n```\n\nPrints \"+Self-Cascading\" and feeds keys at each cursor location.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. No self-cascading.\n2. No feeding keys bypassing `vim.api.nvim__mcursor_cascading`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1823+g 898e6f884e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Btw\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.17.0 (94e7c887)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
