            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "### Off-topic\n\nAnother example of strange self-cascading: the keymap is triggered when moving in Visual mode (`hjkl` trigger `<F1>`).\n\n```text\n<F1>hjkl\n<Esc>\n:messages\n```\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<F1>\", function()\n  vim.notify(tostring(vim.v.cascading), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n  vim.cmd(\"norm! Q*gn\")\n  vim.v.hlsearch = 0\nend)\n```\n\nOn top of the self-cascading, the first cursor does not follow `gn` in the keymap.",
