            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I think the `nvim__mcursor_cascading()` check is done too early.\n\nThis doesn't work for me in the first repro. Something smells fishy here 😾.\n\nIn general, self-cascading might be a strange thing to allow by default:\n\n```\nno cursors -> <key> places cursors -> each placed cursor runs <key>\n```\n\nBut I don't really understand how it works, so I'm not sure.",
